    "name": "Alliston Zachary Esmond Davis",
    "bioEn": "Alliston Davis is a Canadian artist, creator, and cultural connector from Ajax, Ontario, working across music, culture, community, and experiences. A singer-songwriter and multidisciplinary creative, Alliston began his career in acting before expanding into music, event production, community building, and digital storytelling. His creative work is rooted in lived experience, exploring friendship, identity, nightlife, desire, personal growth, and the messy moments that make life worth documenting. Musically, Alliston has moved through R&B, Hip-Hop, Dancehall, Pop, and Alternative, increasingly embracing the energy of 2000s Canadian alternative rock, punk, and pop. His work includes Problematic, Night Pack, 4U, and his latest project, Damn, I Miss You. Beyond music, Alliston has built and produced experiences that bring people together, approaching culture through creativity and connection. His content reflects that same perspective, blending music, lifestyle, humour, relationships, culture, and honest conversations about building a creative life. At the heart of Alliston’s work is a simple belief: you have to experience life to create from it. Whether through a song, an event, a conversation, or a night out with friends, Alliston is building a creative world that celebrates living fully, making meaningful connections, and creating something that feels genuinely yours.",
